{"title":"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems\">2002 AMC 12P #18</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems\">2002 AMC 10P #19</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are real numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/7/6578ddc86a0f881931215ab297dc0b00f32459c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + 2b =7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/1/221b08cebe067874890b9f1a1f8244b2d7fba3a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2 + 4c= -7,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e87b252d0257722b7d81b068192e94ccdd5a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^2 + 6a= -14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5d4539540f356a56e7c14157c8c6d63de830f72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 + c^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/9/829130da58b74d7bb3071c0c6ca69ebca1beb8ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) }14 \\qquad \\text{(B) }21 \\qquad \\text{(C) }28 \\qquad \\text{(D) }35 \\qquad \\text{(E) }49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"378\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Adding all of the equations gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/6/4d6653b44c2520dadaa5fba8b01c7c64e7b10c90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 +c^2 + 6a + 2b + 4c=-14.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"275\" height=\"18\" /> Adding 14 on both sides gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/754fe952697f2eb8d2eccfe386748a3ee79279f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 +c^2 + 6a + 2b + 4c+14=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"292\" height=\"18\" /> Notice that 14 can split into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/6/e96acdb31e027a0280b755e070cd9c75717a103d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9, 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/4054552638cf9f29e857a1306bd3ec31df3c19b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> which coincidentally makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/0/520bc03c7da2248bb815b1d3919f267844410638.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 +6a, b^2+2b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/c/3cc2677f582875bfbfb9aed0aa06c439b463a6d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^2+4c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> into perfect squares. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/1/881a84878e2f1cb930403cd3b0af722ce428afc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+3)^2 + (b+1)^2 + (c+2) ^2 =0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"269\" height=\"21\" /> An easy solution to this equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce999e14f54fe88329c46d254a7a5ec496aac41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=-3, b=-1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/4/264386b2e5d8ceafc02fff26a4be033700ee41a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=-2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" /> Plugging in that solution, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/8/e58acd23ea4b8488cf31eb36e09f3275b35ea20c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2+c^2=(-3)^2+(-1)^2+(-2)^2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 14}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"391\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P\">2002 AMC 10P</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"cen